        "_summary.md": "# Chain Summary: TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_4_v1\n\n**Generated:** 2026-05-05\n**Edit-draft run:** 2026-05-05\n**Status:** PASS (1 issue found and fixed)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Requirements\n\n- **Lesson ID:** TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_4_v1\n- **Curriculum:** Bluebonnet (TX_BBO_XX), Grade 5, Module 1, Lesson 4\n- **Standard:** TEKS 5.6.G; TEKS 5.8.A\n- **Learning Goal:** Students will analyze and describe a theme in \"Shinpei Mykawa.\"\n- **Activity Type:** Close Read\n- **Section Replaced:** Activity Page 4.1 Think-Pair-Share (15 min.)\n- **Anchor Text:** Chapter 4: Becoming a Texas Landowner (~614 words, 11 paragraphs)\n- **TT Format:** Quickwrite ELEM — copy quote + explain (no Claim step per BBO-6)\n- **DQ Count:** 3 (1 MC + 1 verbatim inferential + 1 generated LCQ) — module plan BBO-5 override, binding\n\n### 1a. Verbatim Anchors\n- DQ Verbatim (index 0): \"Why do you think many of Shinpei Mykawa's neighbors had doubts about the success of his rice farm?\"\n- TT Verbatim: none (TT outline only)\n\n### 1b. Cross-Skill Boundaries\n- TT paragraph range restricted to (2)–(8): excludes (9) [DQ3 LCQ anchor], (10) [DQ2 verbatim TDQ anchor], (11) [Check for Understanding territory]\n\n---\n\n## 2. Pedagogical Intent Highlights\n\n- **Tier:** Tier 1 (lesson plan), HIGH confidence\n- **Primary analytical moves:** Identify quotes showing \"opportunity for success in America\"; explain how a quote relates to the theme\n- **Primary relationship type:** HIERARCHICAL SUPPORT — quote serves as evidence for theme (directional; not co-equal)\n- **Verbatim DQ anchors to CONTRAST relationship:** skeptical neighbors vs. confident Mykawa reinforces theme stakes\n- **Cognitive ceiling for DQs:** moderate inference (WHY neighbors doubted) + direct retrieval (potential for prosperity)\n- **Assessment scope:** PRIMARY moves only — quote identification + theme explanation\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exemplars\n\n- **Same-curriculum:** No Bluebonnet entries in Activity Catalog — cross-curriculum fallback triggered\n- **Selected exemplars:** G5_1.0_3 (Fishtank, Seedfolks) and G5_2.0_25 (Fishtank, I Am Malala) — structural reference only; not structural template\n- **Authoritative BBO structural refs:** TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_1_v1 and TX_BBO_XX_G5_1.0_3_v1 draft outputs — took precedence over catalog exemplars\n- **Cross-curriculum guardrails:** Highlight questions, grammar step, Claim+QuickWrite scaffold, and 10+ question count all avoided\n\n---\n\n## 4. Excerpt\n\n- **Selection:** (1)–(11), full Chapter 4 \"Becoming a Texas Landowner\" — author directive\n- **Length:** ~628 words, 11 paragraphs\n- **Numbering:** Sequential from (1) per BBO-7 and excerpt_numbering_rules.md (TX_BBO confirmed sequential)\n- **Italics confidence:** Indeterminate (ArialMT anthology source; no italic markup in activity output per BBO-8)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Final Activity\n\n**Structure:**\n- Type 4 Intro (with concept definition): 4 bubbles, defines \"theme\" verbatim, ends with text redirect\n- Section 1: Driving Questions (3 total)\n  - Q1: mpchoice — What is the theme of Chapter 4? (Answer: B)\n  - Q2: tdq — Why do you think Mykawa's neighbors had doubts? (Verbatim; anchors to P10)\n  - Q3: lcq — What motivates Mykawa and his group per paragraph 9? (Anchors to P9)\n- Type 2 Transition: 1 bubble\n- Section 2: Assessment — QuickWrite (copy quote from (2)–(8) + explain connection to theme)\n- Section 3: Extension — persistence in the face of doubt\n- Type 3 Conclusion: 2 bubbles, Block 1 retrospective, Block 2 \"Now you can:\"\n\n---\n\n## 6. Validation\n\n**All 17 structural checks run. Status: PASS (1 issue fixed)**\n\n| Check | Status | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1. Verbatim Fidelity | PASS | Script confirmed; DQ verbatim placed at Q2 per Position Invariant |\n| 2. Paragraph Reference Integrity | PASS | Q3 references (9); TT references (2)–(8); all within manifest |\n| 3. Question Progression Integrity | PASS | Backward jump Q2(P10)→Q3(P9) accepted per Position Invariant |\n| 4. Assessment Alignment | PASS | QuickWrite ELEM, no Claim, single-quote + explain |\n| 5. Excerpt Completeness | PASS | Full chapter (1)–(11) per author directive |\n| 5b. Source Cross-Reference | PASS | Sequential numbering from (1); no source numbering to preserve |\n| 6. Criteria Quality | FIXED | Extension criteria trimmed from 26 to 18 words; text-return language removed |\n| 7. Brevity | PASS | All questions within type word limits |\n| 8. Content Block Validation | PASS | Type 4 intro ✓, Type 2 transition ✓, Type 3 conclusion ✓ |\n| 9. Question Type Classification | PASS | MC, TDQ, LCQ, QuickWrite, Extension all correctly classified |\n| 10. BBO Curriculum Rules | PASS | BBO-1 through BBO-8 all compliant |\n| 11. Extension Compliance | PASS | Meets Extension Quality Rubric (thematic, one question, low floor/high ceiling) |\n| 12. Grade-Appropriateness | PASS | G5 norms met; DQ count flag expected per module plan override |\n| 13. Paragraph Qualifier Restraint | PASS | No over-qualified paragraph references |\n| 14. TT Insight Protection | PASS | No DQ performs TT analytical move in TT range |\n| 15. Driving Question Mutual Exclusivity | PASS | Q1, Q2, Q3 cover distinct angles; no overlap with TT |\n| 16. Sequential Text Progression | PASS | Position Invariant accepted override documented |\n| 17. Numbering Validation | PASS | Sequential (1)–(11); all references within manifest |\n\n---\n\n## Drift signals to eyeball before accepting this draft\n\n1. **DQ count = 3** — This is intentionally below the G5 default (5–7) and below distilled-patterns.md minimum (4). The module plan explicitly specifies 3 DQs (1 MC + 2 additional), and this is binding per BBO-5. No change needed, but authors should confirm no new module plan version has increased the count.\n\n2. **Backward text order Q2(P10) → Q3(P9)** — The verbatim DQ anchors to paragraph 10 (neighbors' doubts), and the generated LCQ anchors to paragraph 9 (dawn labor motivation). This is correct per the Position Invariant (verbatim placed at first available DQ slot after the module-plan-specified MC), but authors should verify the backward sequence feels natural when reading through the activity.\n\n3. **TT range (2)–(8) excludes P9** — Q3 (LCQ) is anchored to P9 (\"the potential for prosperity\") which is also the richest thematic line. Authors should confirm students won't feel limited by the TT range excluding the most quotable line. Students can still quote from (2)–(8), which contains strong evidence in P8 (deed signing, \"zero reservations\") and P2 (dream formation).\n\n4. **Extension criteria** — Updated from 26 words to 18 words and removed text-return language. Authors should verify the revised criteria (\"Student reflects on what sustains belief or persistence when others doubt, drawing on personal experience or Mykawa's example\") adequately describes acceptable responses.\n",
